;;; world/regions/reedfen.map - Reedfen's rooms, laid out, with one intent
;;; each (harkfell-design section 8). Written before the rooms.
;;;
;;; A1 writes the region's western block: six rooms, three wide and two
;;; deep, at x 8 to 10 and y 3 to 4. The surface (y 3) runs east from the rim
;;; where the Hollow will join; the under-fen (y 4) is reached by falling
;;; and left by climbing. A - or | in the layout joins two rooms: their shared
;;; edge is open (the gates check it); no mark means a closed edge.
;;;
;;;   A Fen Edge    - B Reed Bridge - C Old Stone
;;;   |                               |
;;;   D Root Hollow - E Drowned Channel - F Climb Back
;;;
;;; A3 adds G Behind the Stone (x11y3), east of the Old Stone through its
;;; ring-stone (keyed to H2, which waits in the Drowned Channel).
;;;
;;; The loop: A to B to C, down the hole in C to F, west through E (a swim)
;;; to D, and up the shaft from D to A; or the other way round. Breaths: B
;;; and D (two of six).
(map
  region: reedfen
  origin: (8 3)
  layout:
  ("A-B-C-G"
   "|   |  "
   "D-E-F  ")
  rooms:
  ((A "Fen Edge" "you step off the Hollow's rim and the land opens into reeds and sky")
   (B "Reed Bridge" "the first open water; a breath after the Hollow's climbs")
   (C "Old Stone" "a mute stone seen before it can matter, across a gap that needs a run")
   (D "Root Hollow" "a breath under the reeds: low, dark and still, found by falling")
   (E "Drowned Channel" "too wide to jump: the first swim, bank to bank")
   (F "Climb Back" "rough rock taught where a fall costs nothing, then the climb home to the stone")
   (G "Behind the Stone" "the first place a harmonic opens: a sheltered hollow where moths come to what you carry")))
